given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Haagenson</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuo</surname><given-names>Y-H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Eulerian simulation of tracer distribution during CAPTEX</article-title><source>J. Appl. Meteorol</source><year>1988</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>579</fpage><lpage>593</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b6-ijerph-06-01055"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Platt</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Heagy</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparisons of transport and dispersion model predictions of the URBAN 2000 field experiment</article-title><source>J. Appl. Meteor</source><year>2004</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>829</fpage><lpage>846</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ijerph-06-01055"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nasstrom</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Pace</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of the effect of meteorological data resolution on Lagrangian particle dispersion simulations using the Etex experiment-real-time modeling of airborne hazardous material</article-title><source>Atmos. Env</source><year>1998</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>4187</fpage><lpage>4194</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijerph-06-01055"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Draxler</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of Global and Mesoscale meteorological Model data to Predict the Transport and Dispersion of Tracer Plumes over Washington, D.C</article-title><source>Wea. Forecasting</source><year>2006</year><volume>2